lwsdlgl

Thin C/C++ SDL3 + SDL_GPU + SDL_shadercross wrapper with lwcgl-style Object.function() calls.
SDL handles, structs, enums and flags stay native; no renderer or engine layer is added.

Install dependencies, build and install:

    make deps
    make
    sudo make install

If SDL3 or SDL_shadercross is missing, make prints the exact system/source install path. PREFIX defaults to /usr/local.

Use:

    #include <lwsdlgl/lwsdlgl.h>

    System.init(SDL_INIT_VIDEO | SDL_INIT_GAMEPAD);
    ShaderCross.init();

    SDL_Window *window = Window.create("Game", 1280, 720, SDL_WINDOW_RESIZABLE);
    SDL_GPUDevice *device = GPU.createDevice(ShaderCross.getHLSLShaderFormats(), false, NULL);
    GPU.claimWindow(device, window);

    while (true) {
        SDL_Event event;
        while (Events.poll(&event)) {
            if (event.type == SDL_EVENT_QUIT) goto done;
        }
    }

done:
    GPU.releaseWindow(device, window);
    GPU.destroyDevice(device);
    Window.destroy(window);
    ShaderCross.quit();
    System.quit();

C and C++ use the same header and ABI. Native SDL3 APIs remain available through the included SDL headers.
